{{History of Balisca}}
The '''Continuation War''' ({{lang-bl|Guerra Continuación}}), also known as '''''La Resistencía''''', was a conflict against attempts by the reconstituted [[Community of Volisania]] to forcibly re-impose colonial rule in the [[Northern Triangle]], and it marked the definitive end of the [[Volisanya Boba|''Volisanya Boba'']] period-an extended period of de facto independence that had begun with the [[Volisanian Civil War]]. Although there has been research on the idea of a pan-Baliscan identity that overlapped the early political boundaries, political unification of the [[Northern Triangle]] was not the aim of most, nor was it necessarily inevitable. In fact, there was little coordination between the different factions in the opening years, despite their mutual interest in resisting the Volisan attempt at conquest.

The ambitions of the [[Restaurasionistas|Volisan ''Restaurasionistas'']] to re-assert the authority of the [[Volisanian Empire]] received tactic support from the Bayaran economic elite, in the hopes of preserving {{W|slavery}} (upon which it's profitable {{W|plantation economy}} was based). This support intensified in reaction to the [[Granyana Convention]], in which the [[Northern Confederation]] pledged to "fully eradicate" the practice and [[W:Land redistribution|redistribute land]] to the freedmen. However beyond this, the Bayarans had little affection for the new regime in Volisania. 

Unlike the other [[Abyalan wars of independence]] on the mainland, the ''Resistencía'' was primarily fought to preserve independence already recognized-though informally-by Volisania nearly a century earlier against an attempted imperial ''reconquista'', as opposed to the civil wars between colonists seen in the rest of [[Lurando-Abyala]].

